      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017. Published by Elsevier Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "A 13-year-old boy with a spontaneous vertebrobasilar artery dissecting aneurysm (VADA) in the extracranial artery, which was only 1 mm away from the initial segment of subclavian artery, was successfully treated with a covered-stent to block the artery of the VADA. Our experience indicates that this is a fast, reliable, effective and economical technique, particularly suitable for surgeries in settings with limited resources."
      },
